# aurora.local / packages/documents/pins.env.example
#
# Curated, human-reviewed image pins — the ".example" suffix mirrors the
# existing .env / .env.example convention (see .gitignore): the real
# packages/documents/pins.env is gitignored (generated by `scripts/pin.sh
# --refresh`/`--apply`, host-local), so committed curated recommendations
# live here. Copy or merge into packages/documents/pins.env to adopt.
#
# Every pin below is curated and human-reviewed.
#
# Once adopted as pins.env, this is consumed by scripts/lib/render.sh
# render_pins() into the environment before `docker compose up`. It only
# takes effect in compose.yml image: lines after `scripts/pin.sh --apply`
# has rewritten them to ${IMAGE_<SVC>} — that has NOT been run.
# compose.yml is untouched by this work.
#
# Format: repo:tag@sha256:digest.
#
# Digests obtained with:
#   docker buildx imagetools inspect --format '{{.Manifest.Digest}}' <ref>

# ghcr.io/paperless-ngx/paperless-ngx — latest stable is 3.0.5 (2026-08-01).
# paperless-ngx's own docs recommend pinning to a release *series* (e.g.
# `3.0`) rather than `:latest`, precisely so unattended bugfix upgrades
# don't cross a major version by surprise — this pin goes one step
# further and names the exact patch, with the digest for reproducibility.
# IMPORTANT: v3.0.0 shipped major breaking changes (new Tantivy search
# backend, revised task system, DB migrations) versus the 2.x line. If
# anyone is still running an older 2.x paperless-ngx with real data,
# read the v3.0.0 upgrade notes and back up before adopting this pin —
# it is not a same-for-same patch bump. A fresh install today would
# already land on 3.0.5 (that's what `:latest` currently resolves to),
# so this is not a change in behaviour for a new install. Multi-arch:
# linux/amd64, linux/arm64 — confirmed. Checked 2026-08-15.
IMAGE_PAPERLESS=ghcr.io/paperless-ngx/paperless-ngx:3.0.5@sha256:65a4cabf0169ea7fbd90ab7bb28ba3f8b5909613635acda1a03ad606f34b456b

# docker.io/library/postgres — latest 16.x patch is 16.15-alpine3.24 (the
# `16-alpine` floating tag currently resolves to this on amd64/arm64;
# one lagging platform, riscv64, is still on 16.14 — irrelevant to this
# host). Multi-arch: linux/386, linux/amd64, linux/arm/v6, linux/arm/v7,
# linux/arm64/v8, linux/ppc64le, linux/s390x — confirmed. Checked
# 2026-08-15.
IMAGE_PAPERLESS_POSTGRES=postgres:16.15-alpine@sha256:ab5c955e9e57ae9879d4411ab49a912be9d162455676f7bf56e951b11ac73785

# docker.io/library/redis — latest 7.x patch is 7.4.10-alpine (the
# `7-alpine` floating tag currently resolves to this). Note: Docker
# Hub's official `redis` repo has moved its own `latest`/`8` tags to
# Redis 8, and Redis Ltd changed the core license from BSD to a dual
# RSALv2/SSPLv1 licence starting with Redis 7.4 — worth knowing for
# anyone redistributing this stack, though it does not block
# self-hosted personal use. Staying on the `7` line (as the current
# compose.yml already does) avoids the licence and major-version change
# together; that decision is not revisited here, only pinned precisely.
# Multi-arch: linux/386, linux/amd64, linux/arm/v6, linux/arm/v7,
# linux/arm64/v8, linux/ppc64le, linux/riscv64, linux/s390x — confirmed.
# Checked 2026-08-15.
IMAGE_PAPERLESS_REDIS=redis:7.4.10-alpine@sha256:e7723ff73d963f5cc6d9c4643ea3d989527a402a319239054e9472a7fb9219a2

# docker.io/gotenberg/gotenberg — current compose pins the floating major
# tag `:8`. Latest patch is 8.30.0 (font-stack rewrite: replaced 30+
# font packages with 8 Noto-based ones, ~13% smaller image; no Microsoft
# Core Fonts, metric-compatible replacements substituted instead — worth
# a visual diff check if paperless-ngx PDF output leans on exact font
# metrics, though this is an edge case for most homelab use). Multi-arch:
# linux/386, linux/amd64, linux/arm/v7, linux/arm64, linux/ppc64le —
# confirmed. Checked 2026-08-15.
IMAGE_PAPERLESS_GOTENBERG=docker.io/gotenberg/gotenberg:8.30.0@sha256:d3c9e0ed2450c9a4631de6d14b51c75fd6051512c33aa8a6df622f085592c48b

# docker.io/apache/tika — actively maintained by the Apache Software
# Foundation (this was flagged as a possible "no safe pin" case before
# checking; the check says otherwise). Latest release is 3.3.0.0
# (Tika version 3.3.0, docker build revision 0), pushed 17 days before
# this check. Multi-arch: linux/amd64, linux/arm/v7, linux/arm64,
# linux/s390x — confirmed (note: linux/arm/v7 was dropped starting with
# the 4.0.0-alpha line, so staying on 3.x keeps 32-bit ARM support if
# that ever matters). Checked 2026-08-15.
IMAGE_PAPERLESS_TIKA=docker.io/apache/tika:3.3.0.0@sha256:2a565f1ea1290bdcb74a7d35957d16a989ed44ef98790dcdcc28121d728fa583

# docker.io/frooodle/s-pdf (Stirling PDF) — the project has announced it
# is MOVING this image to `stirlingtools/stirling-pdf` and will eventually
# stop publishing to `frooodle/s-pdf`; today (checked 2026-08-15) both
# names are still being pushed to in parallel, most recently 9 days ago,
# tag 2.14.3. That is still within this task's "about a fortnight" caution
# window and this repo is mid-deprecation, so treat this pin as short-
# lived: re-check before the next update cycle, and the operator should
# plan a deliberate move to `stirlingtools/stirling-pdf` (a different
# image name, so out of scope for a same-image pin — not done here).
# Multi-arch: linux/amd64, linux/arm64 — confirmed.
IMAGE_STIRLING_PDF=docker.io/frooodle/s-pdf:2.14.3@sha256:3b3670fce70b396ec56ba380a3cc7858e0abf83fe13f31c88f7737847763a396
